  "body": "Stacked on #626 (the PathPilot lathe post lives on its branch; this diff shows #626's commits until it merges).\n\n## What changed\n- `assets/posts/fanuc-lathe.cps` and `assets/posts/tormach-lathe.cps`: `endPreamble()` resets `sCss = 0`, so a section's `SurfaceSpeed` PARAM no longer leaks into the next section. A section that states no surface speed after one that did now posts `G97 S<rpm>`, not the stale `G96` with the machine-max cap (Fanuc: before the live-tool early return, so live sections clear it too; Tormach: beside `spinRev = false`).\n- `docs/decisions/772-lathe-css-per-section.md`: the decision and what was dropped.\n\n## How tested\n- Pinning tests (both fail without the fix, pass with it):\n  - `lathe_post_refusals::a_section_without_surface_speed_posts_g97_after_one_with_it` (Fanuc): CSS turning section, then an axial drill with no SurfaceSpeed -> one `G96 S200 M03`, the drill posts `G97 S500 M03`.\n  - `lathe_post_tormach::a_section_without_surface_speed_posts_g97_after_one_with_it` (PathPilot): same stream -> one `G96 D12000 S200 M3`, the drill posts `G97 S500 M3`, LinuxCNC sanity check passes.\n- Locally: `conformance`, `lathe_post`, `lathe_post_refusals`, `lathe_post_tormach`, `lathe_post_tormach_thread`, `c_axis_live` all green; no golden changed (no golden has two sections where one states CSS). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --tests -- -D warnings` clean.\n- Linux quick gate: green on the branch head vs upstream main (app suites, ui suites; 0 failed, 10.2 min).\n\n## Not exercised\n- No app code path writes `PARAM SurfaceSpeed` yet (latent until CSS is wired into the lathe operations), so the change is proved on synthetic streams only; not run on a machine or simulator.\n\nChangelog: Lathe posts (Fanuc, PathPilot): a section's constant surface speed (G96) no longer carries into a later section that states none; that section posts its own G97 rpm (#772)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nfork synced at v0.16.0\n\nFixes #772\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
